# arm64: a fence behind late stores of a new object. `Promise.resolve(v)` in line makes a promise by the stub, which has its fence, and then stores the value and the word that says "fulfilled". A fence of its own follows those two stores where the value may be a cell. x86-64 has no fence at all.
# f1 = made
# -- source: promise-made-fulfilled-has-a-fence-behind-its-value.ts
